## Migration Analysis

Your code has **three** problematic APIs that won't work in .NET 8:

| API | Problem | Pattern |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (`SYSLIB0046` in .NET 9), unreliable | Blocking call interruption |
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` | Cancellable work loop termination |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` without cancellation | Can't be woken cooperatively | Blocking call |

Additionally, there's a **race condition** in the original: if multiple items are enqueued before `WaitOne` returns, `Reset()` is called and subsequent items may be lost since only one `Dequeue` happens per signal.

---

## Migrated Code (.NET 8)

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private Task? _processingTask;
    private CancellationTokenSource? _cts;

    public void Start()
    {
        _cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
        _processingTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
    {
        try
        {
            await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
            {
                Handle(item);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException) when (token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Normal shutdown — exit gracefully
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async Task StopAsync()
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete(); // Signal no more items
        _cts?.Cancel();            // Interrupt if blocked on empty channel

        if (_processingTask is not null)
        {
            // Wait up to 5 seconds for graceful shutdown
            using var timeoutCts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
            try
            {
                await _processingTask.WaitAsync(timeoutCts.Token);
            }
            catch (TimeoutException)
            {
                // Task didn't finish in time — it's cancelled, nothing more to do
            }
        }

        _cts?.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

